+From 24196d4d5e81389a17eeb62a53663f510e298303 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: hamid-enf <85231378+hamid-enf@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 11:11:18 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] Make project fully self-contained: drop HAL, use direct
+ registers
+
+The previous build failed on other machines because the Keil project
+referenced HAL driver sources through absolute paths on the original
+developer's machine (C:/Users/pardazesh/STM32Cube/...). Instead of
+vendoring the whole HAL, the firmware is now bare-metal:
+
+- new stm32f103_regs.h: documented minimal register map (RCC, FLASH,
+  GPIO, TIM1) replacing stm32f1xx.h + HAL types
+- official ARM CMSIS core headers vendored under Drivers/CMSIS/Include
+  (source: @xpack-3rd-party/arm-cmsis-core, CMSIS 5.4.0)
+- tim.c: register-level TIM1 driver (6 complementary outputs, dead time
+  via BDTR, break input), same two modulation modes and config knobs
+- main.c: bare-metal 72 MHz clock setup + modulation ISR
+- gpio.c: register-level pin setup incl. PB12 break input pull-up
+- uvprojx: HAL group + absolute include paths + RTE/pack dependencies
+  removed; only relative paths remain; USE_HAL_DRIVER define dropped
+- deleted HAL leftovers (hal_conf.h, hal_msp.c), CubeMX leftovers (.ioc,
+  .mxproject) and the previous developer's GUI layout file
+- README rewritten with build steps and a learning guide
+
+Verified with a real ARM cross compiler (clang/thumb/Cortex-M3,
+-Wall -Wextra -Werror): all sources compile and link in both
+modulation modes (~1.9 KB flash); BDTR constant (0x5C24 = DT 36 ticks
++ OSSR/OSSI/BKE/AOE) and the TIM1_UP vector entry confirmed in the
+binary; 6 config variants compile clean.
+
+Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
